.SH NAME
\&ag\-cli\-tag\-protection\-delete \- Delete a protected tag rule
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&ag\-cli tag protection delete [<owner>/<repo>] <tag\-or\-pattern> [flags]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Delete a protected tag rule.
.PP
\&By default, the current repository and rule are shown and you will be prompted
\&to confirm. Use \-\-yes to skip the confirmation prompt.
.PP
\&When OWNER/REPO is omitted, the repository is inferred from the current Git repository. An explicit OWNER/REPO argument always takes precedence. Remote selection prefers remote.pushDefault, the current branch upstream, origin, then a unique AtomGit/GitCode remote.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
\&Skip deletion confirmation
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH INHERITED OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
\&Show help for command
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
\&Disable terminal output sanitization for machine processing
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&ag\-cli tag protection delete owner/repo \(dqv*\(dq
\&  ag\-cli tag protection delete owner/repo \(dqv*\(dq \-\-yes
.fi
